// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - StolenTablet 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P918617283" "Tabula Scutum"
// DetailString :
"P2966898835" "When you removed this heavy stone tablet from its pedestal, the background hum in the caves went silent. It still pulses with an unknown power, but it is more contained now, as though it is no longer powering some outside object... or person."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2468968050" "Power from the Past"
// DetailString :
"P2577194103" "The mysterious Sister Airlia hired you for a simple job: break into a Cimeroran shrine and steal a powerful artifact, the <color orange>Tabula Scutum</color>. Your patron didn't offer up the reason why she needed this stone tablet, and you didn't bother to ask her. You just went to the shrine, trashed Legate Cato and took what you wanted."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P463877079" "The mysterious Sister Airlia hired you for a simple job: break into a Cimeroran shrine and steal a powerful artifact, the <color orange>Tabula Scutum</color>. Your patron didn't offer up the reason why she needed this stone tablet, and you didn't bother to ask her why. You just went to the shrine, trashed Legate Cato and took what you wanted.<br><br>It turned out that Sister Airlia didn't want this artifact for herself. She had you travel to St. Martial and deliver it to Ghost Widow. You arrived at the meeting place to find that those pesky Longbow operatives had gotten the drop on Ghost Widow and captured her. You freed her, delivered the Tabula, and returned to Sister Airlia for your reward."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2FailClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3086058945" "The mysterious Sister Airlia hired you for a simple job: break into a Cimeroran shrine and steal a powerful artifact, the <color orange>Tabula Scutum</color>. Your patron didn't offer up the reason why she needed this stone tablet, and you didn't bother to ask her why. You just went to the shrine, trashed Legate Cato and took what you wanted.<br><br>It turned out that Sister Airlia didn't want this artifact for herself. She had you travel to St. Martial and deliver it to Ghost Widow. You arrived at the meeting place to find that those pesky Longbow operatives had gotten the drop on Ghost Widow and captured her. Despite your best efforts, you were unable to free Ghost Widow and deliver the Tabula. Instead, you were forced to to head back to Cimerora and admit your failure to Sister Airlia."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PowerfromthePast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1500208810" "Fragment of Tabula Scutum"
// tDetailString :
"P2467945107" "You finger a fragment of Tabula Scutum, a reminder of a little caper you've come to call<br><br><color deepskyblue>Power from the Past</color><br><br>It all started when Sister Airlia hired you to steal an ancient artifact from a shrine in Cimerora. Getting the Tabula Scutum was the easy part; delivering it was another story. You traveled to St. Martial to drop your loot off with Ghost Widow -- only to find she'd been captured by some Longbow operatives who'd gotten the drop on her.<br><br>You returned to the past and Cimerora to get your reward only to find some meddling heroes had intercepted the artifact before it could be transported to Ghost Window's secret lair. It wasn't your problem but Sister Airlia made it well worth your while to revisit the shrine and destroy the Tabula. Satisfying work for satisfying pay.<br><br>You aren't sure exactly what the connection between Sister Airlia and Ghost Widow is, but it really doesn't matter. Sister Airlia paid you well for the job, and that was the important thing."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2830485637" "The <color orange>Tabula Scutum</color>, a powerful artifact, rests in a well-guarded cave. I would deprive its protector of its power and use that power towards my own ends. In this way I shall weaken a rival and strengthen my own cause. But you need not concern yourself with these details. Simply defeat the guardians and bring the Tabula back to me. Do this, {VillainName}, and you will be well rewarded."
// AcceptString :
"P3163171762" "Steal the Tabula Scutum"
// SendOffString :
"P1700189321" "The Tabula's protector has become worried about its safety and thus dispatched reinforcements to help keep it secure. They are led by <color orange>Legate Cato</color>, a skilled soldier. You should expect some resistance to your efforts to gain the Tabula. Do not let that stop you."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3788623377" "Have you brought me the Tabula?"
// TaskTitle :
"P3534360295" "<color deepskyblue>Power from the Past</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2770291627" "<color deepskyblue>Part One</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4079032271" "The air hums with power emanating from somewhere deep in the cave complex."
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P856364347" ""
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3571567476" "Now we die..."
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P1143315443" "Remain vigilant! The Legate will have our heads if we let our guard down."
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P1484060093" "<shout>Intruder!"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION2 :
"P3836421486" "Aye. Crafty Daedalus is worried he might be deprived of the power of the Tabula. We must not let that happen."
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION2 :
"P267102088" "<shout>Sound the alarm!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3197325112" "Legate Cato"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3287200817" "Be vigilant, for Cimerora can ill afford to have the Tabula fall into the wrong hands."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3364757337" "<shout>A thief! Look alive, men, and make Daedalus proud!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P2216329034" "Ha! It is but a scratch. You will have to do better than that."
// Script Variable BOSS_75HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3659692620" "You fool, do you realize what it is you do?"
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1086462314" "Without the power of the Tabula, noble Daedalus will be hard pressed to support Imperious."
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P720871947" "Stop this madness! You plant the seeds for Daedalus' fall!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P1940010805" "Daedalus, I have failed you! What will become of our Cimerora now?"
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P248534158" "<em victory>Thus is the fate of those who dare steal from Daedalus."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1738482053" "Nevermind"

